---
import LayoutDefault from '~/layouts/LayoutDefault.astro'
---

<LayoutDefault
  title="Our laundry — Shared laundry — Gordan Grgić"
  description="A mobile web project for shared laundry rooms: check machine status before going downstairs. A local prototype, a simulated preview and a future Wi-Fi sensor concept."
>
  <header class="page-heading">
    <a class="back-link" href="/projects/">← All projects</a>
    <p class="folio-label">MOBILE WEB + CONNECTED MACHINES / PROJECT 04</p>
    <h1>Our laundry</h1>
    <p class="lead">Check before you carry the laundry downstairs.</p>
    <a class="try-demo" href="/demos/praonica/">Try the prototype ↗</a>
  </header>
  <div class="project-meta">
    <span>In development</span><span>Brussels · Shared laundry rooms</span><span
      >Mobile web · Python · Wi-Fi concept</span
    >
  </div>
  <section class="laundry-storyboard" aria-label="The idea in two scenes">
    <figure>
      <img
        src="/images/projects/praonica/laundry-before.webp"
        srcset="/images/projects/praonica/laundry-before-800.webp 800w, /images/projects/praonica/laundry-before.webp 1536w"
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 90vw, 45vw"
        width="1536"
        height="1024"
        alt="A frustrated resident with tousled hair and a laundry basket finds both machines occupied"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>
        <span>01 / BEFORE</span><strong>A basket full. Every machine busy.</strong><p>
          You only find out when you get downstairs.
        </p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <img
        src="/images/projects/praonica/laundry-check-phone.webp"
        srcset="/images/projects/praonica/laundry-check-phone-800.webp 800w, /images/projects/praonica/laundry-check-phone.webp 1536w"
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 90vw, 45vw"
        width="1536"
        height="1024"
        alt="The same resident calmly checks her phone at home with the laundry basket beside her"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>
        <span>02 / WITH THE APP</span><strong>A quick check. One less wasted trip.</strong><p>
          Check the machines before leaving your apartment.
        </p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
  <section class="project-story">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>A small everyday frustration.</h2>
      <p>
        In buildings with a shared laundry room, you can carry a full basket downstairs only to find every machine
        occupied. This project starts with a simple question: can residents see the state of the machines before leaving
        their apartment?
      </p>
      <h2>One view, made for a phone.</h2>
      <p>
        The first version focuses on a washing machine and a dryer: running, paused, programme finished, door state and
        an honest indication when the connection is unavailable.
      </p>
      <p>
        A finished programme does not mean an empty machine. An open door does not prove that the laundry has been
        collected. Availability will need a separate, clearly defined confirmation.
      </p>
      <h2>What has actually been checked?</h2>
      <p>
        Development starts with a personally owned washing machine and dryer, used only as test appliances. Read-only
        integration has returned real states for operation, the end of a washing cycle, pause and an open dryer door,
        checked against actual use.
      </p>
      <p>
        A local Python application is being developed around those observations. Its new live integration still needs a
        separate check. The end of a drying cycle, all interruption paths and long-term reliability are not yet
        confirmed.
      </p>
      <h2>A path for other machines.</h2>
      <p>
        For machines without a suitable API, the next idea is a Wi-Fi sensor that observes operation and door events.
        The hardware is a concept, not an installed or tested product. Detection must be checked on each supported
        machine, including pauses and loss of connectivity.
      </p>
      <p>
        The aim is reliable information for residents, without remote starting or stopping. A future building pilot will
        also need private access and a clear way to confirm that laundry has been collected.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="prototype">
      <p class="folio-label">MOBILE PREVIEW / SIMULATED DATA</p>
      <div class="phone">
        <iframe src="/demos/praonica/" title="Simulated mobile laundry prototype" loading="lazy"></iframe>
      </div>
      <p class="preview-note">
        This interactive preview uses simulated examples. It has no connection to real appliances and contains no
        private readings.
      </p>
      <a class="open-demo" href="/demos/praonica/">Open the mobile prototype ↗</a>
    </aside>
  </section>
  <nav class="project-navigation" aria-label="Other projects">
    <a href="/projects/">← All projects</a><a href="/projects/grgagrow/">03 / grgaGrow →</a>
  </nav>
</LayoutDefault>
<style>
  .laundry-storyboard {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 22px;
    margin: 0 0 44px;
  }
  .laundry-storyboard figure {
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 20%, transparent);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .laundry-storyboard img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 3/2;
    background: #f4f4ec;
  }
  .laundry-storyboard figcaption {
    padding: 18px 20px 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 16%, transparent);
  }
  .laundry-storyboard figcaption span {
    display: block;
    font: 10px/1.7 var(--note-font);
    color: var(--note-color);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
  }
  .laundry-storyboard figcaption strong {
    display: block;
    font: 600 17px/1.5 var(--body-font);
  }
  .laundry-storyboard figcaption p {
    font: 13px/1.7 var(--body-font);
    color: var(--note-color);
    margin: 8px 0 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .laundry-storyboard {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 18px;
      margin-bottom: 32px;
    }
  }
  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    font: 11px/1.7 var(--note-font);
  }
  .lead {
    font: 22px/1.5 var(--body-font);
    max-width: 32ch;
    margin-top: 18px;
  }
  .project-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px 22px;
    border-block: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 22%, transparent);
    padding: 16px 0;
    margin: 28px 0 38px;
    font: 11px/1.7 var(--note-font);
    color: var(--note-color);
  }
  .project-story {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 330px), 1fr));
    gap: 42px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .prose {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .prototype {
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: 390px;
    width: 100%;
    justify-self: center;
  }
  .phone {
    width: 100%;
    height: 760px;
    border: 7px solid #283f39;
    border-radius: 30px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #f5f6ef;
    box-shadow: 8px 10px 0 color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 8%, transparent);
  }
  iframe {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border: 0;
    display: block;
  }
  .preview-note {
    font: 11px/1.8 var(--note-font);
    color: var(--note-color);
    margin: 20px 0 12px;
  }
  .open-demo {
    font: 12px/1.7 var(--note-font);
  }
  .try-demo {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 9px 14px !important;
    margin-top: 20px;
    border: 1px solid currentColor;
    font: 600 13px/1.7 var(--note-font);
  }
  .try-demo:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid currentColor;
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .project-navigation {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 40px;
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 20%, transparent);
    font: 12px/1.7 var(--note-font);
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .lead {
      font-size: 20px;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 380px) {
    .phone {
      height: 700px;
      border-width: 4px;
    }
    .project-story {
      gap: 28px;
    }
  }
</style>
